<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
  <!--
    October 2026 Spring Framework advisory wave. The CVE CPE is
    "spring_framework" so dependency-check attributes them to every spring-* jar at the same version
    (spring-core, spring-aop, spring-beans, ...). Suppressions are scoped
    to all org.springframework 6.2-line artifacts since no fixed release
    exists on that line:

      CVE-2026-47883  UrlHandlerFilter / UrlFileNameViewController open redirect (spring-webmvc)
      CVE-2026-47884  XsltView SSRF/RCE (spring-webmvc)
      CVE-2026-47885  PartEventHttpMessageReader maxPartSize (spring-webflux)
      CVE-2026-47886  SpEL power-operator DoS (spring-expression)
      CVE-2026-47887  UrlFileNameViewController open redirect (spring-webmvc)
      CVE-2026-47888  RSocket SETUP frame memory leak (spring-messaging)
      CVE-2026-47889  Jetty12 cookie sameSite (spring-webflux)
      CVE-2026-47890  SSE view-fragment stream corruption (spring-webflux)
      CVE-2026-47891  Aalto XML maxInMemorySize (spring-webflux)
      CVE-2026-47892  functional endpoint header predicate bypass (spring-webflux)
      CVE-2026-47893  WebSocket exception header leak (spring-webflux)
      CVE-2026-59280  FreeMarker path traversal (spring-webmvc freemarker support)
      CVE-2026-59281  data-binding Errors HTML escaping (spring-webmvc)
      CVE-2026-59282  data-binding property-path (spring-beans/context)
      CVE-2026-59283  SpEL SimpleEvaluationContext guard bypass (spring-expression)
      CVE-2026-59313  SSE stream corruption (spring-webmvc)
      CVE-2026-59314  Content-Disposition header splitting (spring-core http pkg)

    Rationale: this library is a DataSource/pool diagnostics starter — it has no
    web layer, does not use SpEL, data binding, RSocket, FreeMarker, SSE, or
    WebSocket, and never builds Content-Disposition headers. The flagged classes
    are unreachable from this artifact. Consumers' own Spring Boot BOM governs
    the actual framework versions at runtime. Revisit on each dependency-check
    run; drop suppressions if a fixed 6.2.x release appears.
  -->
  <suppress>
    <notes>Vulnerable code is in spring-webmvc (UrlHandlerFilter/UrlFileNameViewController); not reachable from this artifact.</notes>
    <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework/spring-[a-z]+@6\.2\..*$</packageUrl>
    <cve>CVE-2026-47883</cve>
  </suppress>
  <suppress>
    <notes>Vulnerable code is in spring-webmvc (XsltView); not reachable from this artifact.</notes>
